      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-04T10:13:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would be convenient, but then you\u0027ll end up registering hundred of devices which I don\u0027t think stuff in device.c is particularly optimized for, there\u0027s even stuff like this in v2.5 (https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/zephyr/+/refs/heads/chromeos-v2.5/kernel/device.c#73, got already reworked in upstream). If the maintainers don\u0027t want extend arguments to sys_init, custom sections may be the way to go, seen it used in some other Zephyr Based SDK as well (the Nordic one).",
      "parentUuid": "d1b920b4_31ba49d8",
      "revId": "2deb82ba576aedea411cb24057f7a00f8d02cb1b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
